# An allowlist at the top level. `/*` ignores every entry in the repository root, and each
# `!/` line below takes one tracked entry back. Everything else a checkout accumulates there
# is ignored without being named. Anything local that must be named belongs in
# .git/info/exclude or a global ignore file, not here: this file is public, and it ships in
# the sdist.
#
# The one rule this adds: a new top-level file or directory needs a `!/` line here, or git
# will not see it. `git status` staying silent about a file you just created at the root is
# the symptom.
#
# `/*` rather than `*`: the slash anchors it to the root, so files inside a tracked directory
# are tracked as they always were, and the patterns further down still apply there. A bare `*`
# would ignore files at every depth and need `!*/` tricks to re-include directories.
/*
!/.github/
!/.gitignore
!/.pre-commit-config.yaml
!/.readthedocs.yaml
!/CHANGELOG.md
!/CITATION.cff
!/CONTRIBUTING.md
!/LICENSE
!/LICENSES/
!/Makefile
!/README.md
!/conda/
!/development/
!/docs/
!/examples/
!/pyproject.toml
!/src/
!/tests/
!/tools/
!/tox.ini
!/utils/

# Inside the tracked directories, at any depth.
.DS_Store
.tox/
.coverage
venv*/
.jupyter/
.ipynb*/
generated/
__pycache__/

# Working notes live alongside the checklist they track, but are not shared. Tracking
# anything else in this directory takes a deliberate negation line below.
/development/*
!/development/RELEASE_CHECKLIST.md

/docs/build/
/docs/development/build/
/docs/user_guide/build/
/docs/user_guide/notebooks/*.ipynb
/docs/user_guide/scripts/plots/*.png
/docs/user_guide/scripts/plots/*.txt
/docs/user_guide/CHANGELOG.md
/docs/user_guide/CONTRIBUTING.md

# generated by `make error-catalog`; build it to read it
/docs/development/source/error_catalog.rst
